NAME
    readpassv - read and verify a secret line twice

SYNOPSIS
    readpassv <prompt> <verify-prompt> [<mismatch-message>]

DESCRIPTION
    readpassv invokes the m-owned readpass command twice, compares the two
    captured values exactly and writes the secret to standard output only when
    they match.

    readpassv is bootstrap-integrated. It resolves readpass from the m system
    command directory supplied by the bootstrap rather than from the inherited
    host PATH.

    If the values differ, the optional mismatch message is written directly to
    /dev/tty and no secret is written to standard output. The command performs
    one verification attempt; it does not retry automatically.

OUTPUT
    On successful verification, standard output contains exactly the secret
    followed by a newline.

    A mismatch produces no standard output. When supplied, mismatch-message is
    written to /dev/tty.

EXIT STATUS
    0   The two values match and the secret was written successfully.
    1   Operational failure, including a readpass failure.
    2   Invalid invocation.
    3   The two entered values do not match.

FILES
    /dev/tty
        Used by readpass for terminal input and by readpassv for an optional
        mismatch message.

SECURITY
    Standard output deliberately carries the verified secret. Callers should
    capture it into a shell variable or connect it only to the intended
    consumer.

EXAMPLES
    password=$(readpassv 'Password: ' 'Repeat password: ' \
        'Passwords do not match.') || exit $?

SEE ALSO
    readpass
